Left by k364. 13 files still carry a =head1 FUNCTIONS or METHODS block at the end of the file: OCP.pm, OCP::Cmd::Apply::AMDGPU, OCP::Drift, OCP::ErrorLine, OCP::K8s, OCP::Keys, OCP::Kubeconfig, OCP::Node, OCP::Password, OCP::Rex, OCP::Share, OCP::StateDir, OCP::Versions. House format is inline =func/=method next to each sub.

Why it is not a find/replace: in @Author::GETTY, =func and =method are only a =head2 shortcut with no collector, so converting an __END__ block in place drops the FUNCTIONS heading from the built POD. k364 tried it on ErrorLine and StateDir and the dzil build before/after comparison showed the lost heading.

Done = the POD sits inline per sub, and a dzil build before/after (pod2text per built file) shows no lost content.

